[COMMENTS]
STATION,GRP flat V Crump weir built in 1989 affected by siltation in upstream section. GENERAL: Station was built in 1989. GRP flat V Crump weir, 3m wide. Station number previously 44801. STATION HYDROMETRY: Frequent silt / gravel accumulation occurs upstream of the weir and in approach channel. No known modularity problems. One peak flow rating applied across period of record. FLOW RECORD: Digital POT and AMAX data (from 01/01/1992) are presented. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7) and in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Some spring abstraction. Fish farm upstream of station.
CATCHMENT,The catchment area consists mainly of Upper Cretaceous, Upper Chalk and Upper Greendsand. Top end is a chalk stream. Land use mostly rural. No major catchment changes.
Qmed Suitability,Rating expected to perform well to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED.
[END]
